        "listed_on": "2026-11-18T06:30:00Z",
        "label": "Notice when something shows up, and tell the engine",
        "job": "Keep watching for things outside (a stretch of time passing, a drive attached or removed, files someone finished putting in a place, a delivery over the network) and tell the person's engine one fact each time, so any tool whose wake hears that kind of fact starts",
        "description": "Give waiters: the standing orders the noticer keeps (notice-when-something-shows-up.waiter-descriptor rows, each naming one mechanism in do-work/mechanisms, its settings and the kind of fact it emits). It runs as a kept-open program: while its wake is on, each waiter waits, and each time something shows up or goes away it tells the engine one fact at wake:arrive, of the waiter's kind, with the change's fields as text. A tool hears it by declaring a wake {fact: {kind, from: [\"run\"], match}}. This row may tell only the kinds its rights name. Each fact told or refused is one line of the program's output. Given for_seconds, it watches that long and answers {told, refused}. A second wake, keep-noticing-row-changes, watches one database's changes (the row-changes leaf) over the connection the person keeps under own-rows-postgres-connection; it is off until the person switches it on, and only then does the run hold that connection and reach its host.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "waiters": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "kind",
                  "id",
                  "is_active",
                  "mechanism_capability_ref",
                  "mechanism_leaf",
                  "emitted_record"
                ]
              },
              "minItems": 1
            },
            "for_seconds": {
              "type": "number",
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "description": "Watch this long, then answer every fact told; left out, it watches until it is stopped (its wake keeps it running)."
            },
            "credential_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The vault name of a database connection (postgresql://…?sslmode=verify-full) a row-changes waiter reads, handed to the run on descriptor 4; only that connection's hosts are reached."
            }
          },
